  "implemented": [
    "Nullable durable closure marker is written only by the trusted original coordinator protocol after its exact settled physical hold is ready; no marker for historical raw/unmarked states.",
    "Foreign custodian uses its own activated funded binding, verified JWT admin, strict action/operation/revision DTO and fixed no-store errors.",
    "One closed-enum administrative transaction engine keeps original preparing1-to-released2 abort and witnessed closing-to-released successor; action UUID namespace is shared across audit tables.",
    "Original allocated quantities, released CAS and owner-written audit commit once; process metadata credits are never released.",
    "Observed missing/underflowed usage invalidates the local accounting basis even after rollback; no silent repair or fresh admission while uncertain.",
    "Additive schema v6 preserves checksums1-5; historical v5 rows remain unmarked; audit runtime SELECT-only survives later generic grants."
  ],
  "evidence_boundaries": [
    "Actual pinned PostgreSQL18.6 and real JWT HTTP composition with two logical nodes; resource observations/transport are controlled.",
    "Two actually spawned owned Python coordinator processes close real data SQL and exit before/after durable marker; only the marker permits foreign resource release, never PID absence.",
    "Faults cover original-fence lost acknowledgement, finalizer postcommit transport/interface/storage-close/binding uncertainty, precommit usage/binding rollback, global cross-kind action IDs and unchanged metadata.",
    "569 distinct cases in one final execution, no FAIL/ERROR/SKIP; earlier intermediate results are history and are not added to the total.",
    "The 119PASS/3FAIL intermediate run had three new test expectation/mocking errors; strengthened total/control/SQL-loan assertions and corrected exception arity without changing product code for those fixture failures."
  ],
